      "id": "claim_6f878e22bb5c4e849fbde64563a92481",
      "statement": "The rate limiter is a reusable DB-backed per-subject fixed-window primitive whose default subject is the verified bearer id; anonymous callers resolve to None and skip the limit, and a client-supplied id is never used as the subject by default because it is spoofable and shares the auth id space.",
